#
# The coprocessor's watchdog feeder no longer looked after, at an orderly shutdown - scripts/xgs/feeder.py.
#
# After the kernel follower's rebuild (20-octep, and os-kernelfollow's 21-kernelfollow, each up to ten
# minutes on the reboot that brings a new kernel), before the host's own watchdog is disarmed
# (23-xgs-watchdog) and before 80-freebsd takes the management link down with the network. Until
# 2026-11-06 this was 07: the coprocessor went unwatched through the whole rebuild, and a feeder that
# stopped in it, or a Linux that hung, went on to the coprocessor's own reset, which an XGS 3300's host
# does not come back from.
SCRIPT=/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/xgs/feeder.py
[ -f "${SCRIPT}" ] || exit 0
/usr/local/bin/python3 "${SCRIPT}" stop > /dev/null 2>&1
exit 0
